<title>ITALY: Italy govt to discuss ERM at TV &quot;question time&quot;.</title>
<headline>Italy govt to discuss ERM at TV &quot;question time&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government will answer questions on the lira's return to the Exchange Rate Mechanism in parliament in a televised &quot;question time&quot; session at 1600 GMT on Thursday, parliamentary sources said.</p>
<p>The lira returned to the European currency grid on Monday after a four-year absence. Its central parity was set at 990 per mark in marathon talks between finance ministers and central bank officials in Brussels at the weekend.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
